## Summary

**Tenth refactoring — centralized the "legacy Android" version check in `ViewUtil.java`.**

The condition `VERSION.SDK_INT <= 19` was repeated across **5 methods** (`disableMarquee`, `enableMarquee`, `setTextScrollSpeed`, `enableTransparentDialog`, `enableLeftDialog`), three of them carrying a duplicated `// Android 4: Broken grid layout fix` comment. The bare `19` is a magic number (API 19 = Android 4.4 KitKat) and the "skip this tweak on old Android" intent had to be re-inferred at each site.

I introduced:
```java
/** API level of the last Android 4.x release (4.4 KitKat). */
private static final int LAST_LEGACY_API = 19;

/**
 * Android 4.x (API 19 and below) has broken grid layout, marquee and dialog rendering;
 * several of the view tweaks below are skipped on those versions.
 */
private static boolean isLegacyAndroid() {
    return VERSION.SDK_INT <= LAST_LEGACY_API;
}
```
and replaced all five conditions with `isLegacyAndroid()`. The rationale that was scattered in inline comments now lives once in the helper's javadoc, so the magic number and the "why" are defined in a single place.

**Behavior-preserving:** `isLegacyAndroid()` evaluates to exactly `VERSION.SDK_INT <= 19`; each site is a one-for-one substitution of the equivalent sub-expression (the `textViews == null` / `context == null || rootView == null` parts of the compound conditions are untouched). Verified no stray `SDK_INT <= 19` literals remain outside the helper and that `VERSION` is still used/imported.

Net: **+10 / −5 lines** (the growth is the helper + doc), with the version threshold now defined once instead of five times.

